CMD commands:
- set - check the path
- ver - system version
- systeminfo - info about system
- cls - clears page
- ipconfig - network information
- ipconfig /all - more info about network
- ping <target_name> - checks if we can access a network server
- tracert <target_name> - tracks the network route
- nslookup <target_name> - shows the IP adress
- netstat -abon - current connections and listening ports
- cd - current directory
- dir - child directories
- dir /a - also hidden directories
- dir /s - files in current directory
- tree - tree representation of files
- cd <directory> - changes directory
- cd .. - goes up one level
- mkdir - create directory
- rmdir - delete directory
- type - view file
- more - view bigger file
- copy <file> <new_file> - copies a file
- move <file> <location> - moves a file
- del <file> - deletes a file
- copy *.md - copies all files that are md
- tasklist - running processes
- tasklist /FI "imagename eq sshd.exe" - all processes related to sshd.exe
- taskkill /PID <task_id> - kills the process
- chkdsk - chcecks the file system for errors
- driverquery - list of all installed drivers
- sfc /scannow - scans system files for corruption

PowerShell commands:
- Get-Command - lists available commands
- Get-Command -CommandType "Function" - lists all commands that are functions
- Get-Help <cmdlet> - help about query
- Get-Help <cmdlet> -examples - common examples
- Get-Alias - list of available aliases
- Find-Module -Name "PowerShell" / -Name "Remove*"- searches for this module from online repositories
- Install-Module -Name "PowerShellGet" - we found a module and we want to install it now
- Get-ChildItem - lists all subfolders
- -Path - specifies the Path
- Set-Location - changes directory
- New-Item -Path <path> -ItemType <type> - creates sth new
- Remove-Item -Path <path> - deletes an item
- Copy-Item -Path <path> -Destination <dest> - copies an item
- Move-Item -Path <path> -Destination <dest> - moves an item
- Get-Content -Path <path> - shows whats in the file
- | - piping two commands ex. Get-ChildItem | Sort-Object Length
- Sort-Object <crit> - sorts objects
- Get-ChildItem | Where-Object -Property "Extension" -eq ".txt" - specified condition
  - ne - not equal
  - gt - greater than
  - ge - greater or equal to
  - lt - less than
  - le - less or equal to
  - like - has sth in it ex. "ship*"
- Get-ChildItem | Select-Object Name,Length / -First 1 - shows things we only need
- Select-String -Path ".\captain-hat.txt" -Pattern "hat" - searches for hat in a file
- Get-ComputerInfo - computer info
- Get-LocalUser - all accounts
- Get-NetIPConfiguration - info about networks
- Get-Process - list of all working processes
- Get-Service - list of services
- Get-NetTCPConnection - displays current TCP connections
- Get-FileHash -Path .\ship-flag.txt - gets file hash
- Get-Item -Path "C:\House\house_log.txt" -Stream * - info about file
- Invoke-Command - runs commands on computers or servers

Linux commands:
- pwd - actual directory
- cd - change directory
- ls - list subdirectories
- cat <file> - show content of a file
- grep <looking for> <file> - look for specified word
- Invoke-Command -ComputerName RoyalFortune -ScriptBlock { Get-Service } - remote commands



